    "## 4. Standardize categories and resolve repeat records\n",
    "\n",
    "* Normalize smoking labels (`Y`, `yes`, `1`) and states (`CA`, `ca`, `CA `).\n",
    "* Retain missing values for explicit imputation within each training fold.\n",
    "* Without encounter dates, we cannot tell which duplicated record is most recent. For this take-home, keep the first record per patient, consistently across all steps. This avoids patient overlap and prevents repeated patients from receiving higher statistical weight. In a real system, request timestamps and rebuild one valid pre-index snapshot per patient."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "58491b17",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-09T03:18:43.522600Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-09T03:18:43.522494Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-09T03:18:43.591055Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-09T03:18:43.590486Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "46,000 distinct patients | 17 model features\n",
      "Categorical: ['sex', 'state', 'smoker']\n",
      "Numerical: ['age', 'n_chronic_conditions', 'has_chf', 'has_copd', 'has_diabetes', 'has_ckd', 'n_encounters_last_year', 'n_ed_visits_last_year', 'prior_inpatient_admission', 'n_active_medications', 'hba1c', 'egfr', 'bmi', 'systolic_bp']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def clean_categories(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    frame = frame.copy()\n",
    "    frame['sex'] = frame['sex'].astype('string').str.strip().str.upper().fillna('UNKNOWN')\n",
    "    frame['state'] = frame['state'].astype('string').str.strip().str.upper().fillna('UNKNOWN')\n",
    "    frame['smoker'] = (frame['smoker'].astype('string').str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "                       .replace({'y': 'yes', '1': 'yes', 'n': 'no', '0': 'no'})\n",
    "                       .fillna('unknown'))\n",
    "    return frame\n",
    "\n",
    "patients = clean_categories(raw.drop_duplicates(subset=ID, keep='first').reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "to_score = clean_categories(score_raw)\n",
    "assert patients[ID].is_unique\n",
    "assert patients[TARGET].isin([0, 1]).all()\n",
    "\n",
    "EXCLUDED = [ID, TARGET, SUSPECT_FEATURE]\n",
    "FEATURES = [c for c in patients.columns if c not in EXCLUDED]\n",
    "CATEGORICAL = ['sex', 'state', 'smoker']\n",
    "NUMERIC = [c for c in FEATURES if c not in CATEGORICAL]\n",
    "assert not set(EXCLUDED).intersection(FEATURES)\n",
    "print(f'{len(patients):,} distinct patients | {len(FEATURES)} model features')\n",
    "print('Categorical:', CATEGORICAL)\n",
    "print('Numerical:', NUMERIC)"
   ]
  },
